hls: a subtitle request is sent once and given up after 2 s without data

The subtitle segments are read by the same hls_read_packet() call that
reads the audio and video, so a subtitle server that stalls holds the
media for the whole I/O timeout of each request and its http retries
(0070), about 32 s with the caller's 8 s rw_timeout.

Open the subtitle playlist reloads and segments with an I/O timeout of at
most 2 s and without http's reconnects. A subtitle playlist reloads on a
connection of its own, so the media playlist's kept-alive connection keeps
its own timeout; a stalled subtitle request then fails within 2 s, as 0078
handles it.

